{
  "abstract": "We develop a conditional fixed-point framework for gradient flows on internal fiber products of smooth bundles over a base manifold. The fibers are compact and have uniformly bounded geometry. We construct spectral-bundle projections onto the joint harmonic sector and study flows generated by coercive analytic energies on the internal fiber product. The paper establishes the geometric and anisotropic Sobolev setting, uniform first-order Sobolev bounds for the coherent projector, analytic-semigroup well-posedness and smoothing, projected fixed-point existence by variational, Schauder, or Darbo methods, coherent uniqueness under strong convexity or a clean spectral-gap reduction, quantitative Galerkin approximation, explicit examples, and \u0141ojasiewicz\u2013Simon convergence. All results are analytic and control-theoretic statements under the displayed hypotheses. The Riemannian base is not automatically physical Lorentzian spacetime, the flow parameter is not automatically physical time, and the abstract fiber product does not by itself select the canonical MTT internal topology.",
